implementationPlan.description:
Verify once. get_context is a shared wire contract, so run the FULL gate fresh, in an isolated Linux snapshot of HEAD:
- whole-repo git archive, overlaying only this task's files plus the landed C06a module if it is not yet in HEAD;
- native deps, MOE_* unset, Linux-only PATH (mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate).
The gate is `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test` plus `npx tsc --noEmit`, and both must exit 0. cmp the overlaid files first. Supply the npm test command, exit code and output tail to complete_task.

Mutants, on scratch copies, each restored and cmp'd afterwards:
1. store a base without an epoch: D5;
2. skip the lastPhaseAt check, by passing a stale current: D7;
3. a process-global store instead of the WeakMap: D4;
4. emit contextDelta on legacy reads: D8.
Keep the diff at or under 400 net lines.

comments.content:
Planning verdict (architect-4c57a52b, 2026-10-26): not plannable yet. I'm parking it on its real prerequisites with report_blocked, not writing a speculative plan.

Why:
1. The declared dependency C05 (negative search provenance) is BLOCKED and unplanned. It extends C04's positive cache, which is blocked on C03 (blocked on R10) and C02b (blocked on R09). The rollout's delta contract (docs/plans/2026-10-24-ai-code-quality-and-context.md, "Session deltas and context receipts") puts "updated source references" and "new evidence" in every delta. Their change identity is the provenance and generation contract that C04 and C05 define.
2. DoD2 needs a full snapshot on "VM replacement" and a delta bound to the "receiver process incarnation". The isolated session's fresh-session identity is an R10 deliverable (Isolated agent lifecycle), and R10 is BACKLOG behind R09.

When it returns to PLANNING, plan against these landed pieces:
- C01's compact packet;
- F06's served-context identity (get_context sessionId, servedContext, receipts and packetId);
- F09-F12a's proxy-stamped session and attempt identity;
- R10's incarnation identity;
- C04 and C05's provenance fields.

Open design questions for that plan:
- How the daemon learns of a compaction. The moe-compaction-keeper mod's session.compact hook is the only seat-side signal today.
- That reattach_attempt keeps the generation and must not count as a base acknowledgement (DoD3).
